After `git add -N` records intent-to-add for only the packet-owned baseline and
evidence paths, `git diff --check` exits 0 and `git diff --name-status` lists
only those allowed paths. This makes the whitespace/scope sweep meaningful in a
new zero-commit repository without creating a content commit.

